  { id: "ca-2026-02-002-437", category: "Sports", question: "What is the name of the mission launched to promote Assam’s famous Muga Silk?", options: ["Mission Resham", "Mission Purvodaya", "Mission Senehjori", "Mission Vastra"], answer: 2, explanation: "Financial Outlay: Estimated investment of ₹396–411 crore.\n\nQ: What is unique about Muga Silk compared to other silks?\nAnswer: It is a wild silk produced only in Assam, known for its natural shimmering golden-yellow color and extreme durability (it often outlasts the lifespan of the wearer).\n\nQ: Which insect produces Muga Silk, and what does it feed on?\nAnswer: It is produced by the silkworm Antheraea assamensis, which feeds primarily on Som (Machilus bombycina) and Soalu (Litsea polyantha) leaves.\n\nQ: What legal protection does Assam's Muga Silk hold?\nAnswer: It was granted the Geographical Indication (GI) tag in 2007, ensuring that only silk produced in the region can legally use the name."}

